{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1vUetJDx9JKihWxCM4X", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with a PASS verdict at confidence 0.4. That verdict is weak: two real bugs were confirmed, and several areas went untested.\n\n**Confirmed and logged (developer confirmed both):**\n1. **Single-step replace ignores regex backreferences.** With regex on, searching `(cat)@home` and replacing with `$1@work` turned `cat@home dog@home` into `$1@work dog@home` instead of `cat@work dog@home`. \"Replace all\" handles `$1` correctly, so the bug is specific to the single-step path. This matches the changelog's note about the plain-string path.\n2. **View mode drops dollar signs.** Money.md contains `Costs $5 and $10`, but View mode renders `Costs 5 and 10`. The edit view still holds the original text.\n\n**Filed but not reproduced (developer could not reproduce):**\n3. **Move line up/down can insert a blank line and drop the trailing newline.** My first attempt gave `- item\\n\\n  - child`. The developer could not reproduce it, and my clean reruns swapped lines correctly. The one bad case that repeated looked like the cursor was on the empty line after the trailing newline, where the result is actually correct. This one is unverified.\n\n**Checked and working:**\n- Sort: Name, Date, and Size with Reverse order and Folder first; the choice persists when navigating.\n- Editor: Move line down swaps correctly; each move undoes in one step.\n- Plain replace (including `$` in the search) and undo; regex Replace all.\n- View mode: nested lists, `cat@home`, and plain text render correctly; rotation keeps content.\n\n**Not covered:**\n- MIME type and Folder local sorts, the .dotfiles toggle.\n- Date and Size reverse order with real timestamp differences, since all files share one timestamp.\n- Go to, Preserve Case, file create/rename, and whether sort survives an app relaunch.\n\n**Side effects:** A stray keyboard tap typed characters into Indent.md and Indent2.md; I undid them and both files match their saved content. I left the sort at Name ascending, as it was at the start."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 724, "cache_read_input_tokens": 311271, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 724}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ef4a079f-183d-4d11-9aa4-b612a2668da1", "uuid": "72696c09-bd97-4fed-8192-bf48c7a87ed4", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T01:05:40.956Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1vUeeA5JKTtxPFxdZvq"}
